{"text": "TORTS I: SYLLABUS\nFALL 2020\n\nProf. David Logan\ndlogan@rwu.edu\n\nCOURSE COVERAGE\n\nTorts | is 3-credits, in the fall semester (Torts II is 2-credits in the spring)\n\nIn Torts | we will cover:\n\nA. Background Memo #1: Torts |: Course Overview-FALL 2020\n\nB. Background Memo #2: What in the Heck is Torts?\n\nC. INTENTIONAL TORTS\n\n1. Background Memo #3: Introduction to Intentional Torts\n\n2. The Prima Facie Intentional Torts Case\n\na.\nb.\n\nIntent (Case Book (\u201cCB\u201d) pp. 17-31)\nBattery (including Transferred Intent) (CB 31-39)\nAssault (CB 39-42)\nFalse Imprisonment (CB 42-51)\nIntentional Infliction of Emotional Distress (CB 53-72)\n\nTrespass to Land/Nuisance/Trespass to Chattels/Conversion (CB 72-\n76; 79-82)\n\n2. Defenses to Intentional Tort Claims\n\na.\n\nConsent (CB 97-110) + Background Memo #4: Consent and Sex\n\nb. Self Defense/Defense of Others (CB 110-13)\n\nCc.\n\nd.\n\nDefense of Property (CB 114-20)\nNecessity (CB 126-32)\n\n3. Torts Remedies\n\na. Background Memo # 5: Damages: Compensatory & Punitive",
